The legal texts come from LiberLII, the Liberia Legal Information Institute (www.liberlii.org), read through the
Internet Archive's Wayback Machine (web.archive.org) from captures made between 2017 and 2026, retrieved
28 October 2026:

  Constitution of the Republic of Liberia (1986); Penal Law, Title 26, Liberian Code of Laws Revised;
  Freedom of Information Act of 2010.

LiberLII publishes no licence for its legislation pages. They are the public law of the Republic of Liberia,
reproduced with the attribution above; their copyright status is not confirmed here. The dates of the Constitution
are from WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/en/legislation/details/8556).

Changes made by Lexifina: each text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph or item per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; tables of contents were left out; LiberLII's dated editorial notes were
moved from the text into the commit messages; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws
that made each change, where the source names them. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither LiberLII nor the
Government of Liberia endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
